Bootstrap: localimage
From: /net/software/containers/universal.sif

# SO3LR-only sidecar container — the JAX/orbax SO3LR MLFF family.
#
# WHY a sidecar (same story as deps/uma_sidecar.def):
#   SO3LR is JAX-based (jax / flax / jax-md / glp) and requires Python >=3.12.
#   The main quantum_chem-*.sif is a torch stack on Python 3.11 (MACE 0.3.15,
#   SCINE, AIMNet2, ...). The two can't share one env, so SO3LR runs here and
#   everything else stays in quantum_chem.sif. SO3LR is PBE0+MBD-lineage, so it
#   is an INDEPENDENT cross-check on the OMol25-trained families (mace-omol /
#   mace-polar / uma / esen).
#
# WHAT'S INSIDE:
#   A uv-managed Python 3.12 venv at /opt/so3lr-venv with jax[cuda12] + the
#   staged SO3LR *v2-beta* package (so3lr 0.2.0). The package source is copied
#   in at build time via %files (below), so the build does NOT depend on /net
#   being bound during %post, and the image is self-contained (the bundled
#   so3lr-{s,m,l} weights install into site-packages). %environment puts the
#   venv first on PATH, so `python` inside the image is the 3.12 SO3LR python.
#
# BUILD (~15-25 min, downloads jax + CUDA wheels):
#   cd /home/woodbuse/codebase_projects/quantum_cowboy_biochemistry
#   apptainer build --fakeroot \
#       /net/software/containers/users/woodbuse/quantum_chem/so3lr-$(date +%Y%m%d).sif \
#       deps/so3lr_sidecar.def
#
# RUN — the factory (_make_so3lr) globs for so3lr-*.sif here and, when so3lr is
# not importable in the caller's Python, prints the apptainer-exec line to use:
#   apptainer exec --nv --bind /home --bind /net \
#       /net/software/containers/users/woodbuse/quantum_chem/so3lr-YYYYMMDD.sif \
#       python -m quantum_engine.cli <op> --model so3lr-m ...

%labels
    Author woodbuse@uw.edu
    Project cowboy-quantum-chemistry
    Purpose SO3LR (JAX) sidecar — so3lr is JAX-based + Python>=3.12, can't live in the torch container

%files
    # Copy the staged v2-beta SO3LR source into the image (host /net is mounted
    # at build time, so this works without a build-time bind). pip installs it
    # in %post — the bundled so3lr-{s,m,l} weights come along into site-packages.
    /net/databases/huggingface/mlFF_models/models--general-molecular-simulations--so3lr-v2-beta/package/so3lr_ts_pipeline/so3lr_folder /opt/so3lr_src

%post
    set -e

    # ── 1. uv (fast resolver) + a clean Python 3.12 venv ────────────────────
    # universal.sif is Python 3.11; SO3LR requires >=3.12, so uv fetches a
    # standalone 3.12 and builds an isolated venv (the INSTALL.md approach).
    pip install --no-cache-dir uv || {
        curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
        export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
    }
    uv venv --python 3.12 /opt/so3lr-venv
    . /opt/so3lr-venv/bin/activate

    # ── 2. JAX (GPU) + the staged SO3LR package ─────────────────────────────
    # jax[cuda12] ships the CUDA runtime via pip wheels (no system CUDA needed).
    # Installing so3lr pulls ASE, numpy, jraph, jax-md, glp, orbax, ...
    uv pip install "jax[cuda12]"
    uv pip install "/opt/so3lr_src/."

    # ── 3. Sanity check — fail the build if the import is broken ─────────────
    python - <<'PY'
import sys, so3lr, jax, ase, numpy
from so3lr import So3lrCalculator                 # lazy alias -> make_ase_calculator
from so3lr.model_registry import available_models
print(f"  python  {sys.version.split()[0]}")
print(f"  so3lr   {so3lr.__version__}")
print(f"  jax     {jax.__version__}  devices={jax.devices()}")
print(f"  ase     {ase.__version__}   numpy {numpy.__version__}")
print(f"  bundled models: {available_models()}")
print("  So3lrCalculator import OK")
PY

%environment
    # Put the SO3LR venv first so `python` == the 3.12 SO3LR interpreter.
    export PATH=/opt/so3lr-venv/bin:$PATH
    export HF_HOME=/net/databases/huggingface
    # SO3LR uses float64 for TS work; enable JAX x64 by default for callers.
    export JAX_ENABLE_X64=1

%test
    /opt/so3lr-venv/bin/python -c "from so3lr import So3lrCalculator; from so3lr.model_registry import available_models; print('SO3LR sidecar OK:', available_models())"

%help
    SO3LR sidecar (JAX, so3lr 0.2.0 / v2-beta).

    Use this image only for SO3LR (`--model so3lr` / so3lr-s / so3lr-m / so3lr-l)
    calls. Everything else (MACE, ORB, AIMNet2, SCINE, propka, UMA, ...) lives in
    the main quantum_chem.sif / the UMA sidecar and is NOT available here.

    The central staged weights are at
      /net/databases/huggingface/mlFF_models/models--general-molecular-simulations--so3lr-v2-beta/
    and quantum_engine/site.py points each alias at weights/<size>/params.pkl;
    quantum_engine.calc.factory._make_so3lr derives the workdir from that.

    Example single-point on so3lr-m (charge read from atoms.info['charge']):

      apptainer exec --nv --bind /home --bind /net \
        /net/software/containers/users/woodbuse/quantum_chem/so3lr-YYYYMMDD.sif \
        python -c "
      import numpy as np
      from ase.io import read
      from so3lr import So3lrCalculator
      calc = So3lrCalculator(model='so3lr-m', lr_cutoff=100.0, dtype=np.float64)
      a = read('in.pdb'); a.info['charge'] = -2; a.calc = calc
      print(a.get_potential_energy())
      "
